### Run core Infection developer commands (composer install, make targets, PHPUnit, infection CLI)

Source: https://github.com/infection/infection/blob/master/AGENTS.md

Core developer commands for the Infection project. `make autoreview` is the definition of done; PHP floor is 8.3. Use `make cs` for formatting, never hand-format. Run a single test file or method with the vendor PHPUnit binary, and use `./bin/infection` for running from source or describing a mutator.

```bash
composer install
make help                 # the definitive list of targets
make cs                   # PHP-CS-Fixer; ALWAYS this, never hand-format
make autoreview           # cs-check + PHPStan(+PHPat) + Mago + composer validate
                          #   + AutoReview suite + Rector dry-run + collision detector
                          #   + zizmor (locally only; CI skips it here)
make test-unit            # default group, e2e excluded
make test-unit-parallel   # paratest WrapperRunner
make test-e2e             # PHPUnit-group e2e + scripted scenarios
make test-infection       # dogfood: Infection on itself (needs the PHAR)
make compile              # build the scoped PHAR (Box + PHP-Scoper)

vendor/phpunit/phpunit/phpunit tests/phpunit/Path/To/SomeTest.php   # one file
vendor/phpunit/phpunit/phpunit --filter test_method_name           # one method
./bin/infection --threads=max                                      # run from source
./bin/infection describe Plus                                      # explain a mutator
```

--------------------------------

### Use expectException*() API for exception tests (PHP)

Source: https://github.com/infection/infection/blob/master/adr/0004-PHPUnit-expect-exception-over-try-catch.md

PHPUnit's exception-expectation API for asserting exception type, message, or code. Other expectException*() assertions may also be used.

```php
function test_something(): void
{
    // ...

    // Other expectException*() assertions may also be used.
    $this->expectException($exception);

    // The statement that fails
}
```

--------------------------------

### Avoid try-catch in tests (PHP)

Source: https://github.com/infection/infection/blob/master/adr/0004-PHPUnit-expect-exception-over-try-catch.md

Shows the pattern using try-catch that must not be used. The fail() assertion is required to avoid false positives when no exception is thrown.

```php
function test_something(): void
{
    // ...

    try {
        // The statement that fails

        // This assertion is required if the statement does not throw.
        $this->fail();
    } catch (Exception $e) {
        // ...
    }
}
```

--------------------------------

### Declare environment variable with #[WithEnvironmentVariable] attribute

Source: https://github.com/infection/infection/blob/master/adr/0011-use-phpunit-environment-variable-attribute.md

Use this attribute on a test class or method to declare a required environment variable. PHPUnit sets the variable before the test and restores previous getenv() and $_ENV values afterwards. Note that $_SERVER is not populated or backed up.

```php
#[WithEnvironmentVariable('EXAMPLE_VARIABLE')]
final class ExampleTest extends TestCase
{
}
```
